model shift_hole
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, M2 C2, item 9 (pick P5): add_business past the calendar's edge with a hole on the way. cal_h is governed in 2026 only, so every day outside 2026 reads a hole (HOLE-UNGOVERNED). n business days move at least n days, so h_back and h_fwd pass the edge whatever the hole: decided without it (L §8.1), refused (R2, L §8): RUN-LIMIT. Twins: the same shifts over cal, governed always (s_back, s_fwd); shifts that land inside the edge, where the hole decides (h_in2) or isn't met (h_in)"

source plan "plan"

input d: date

input cal: calendar

input cal_h: calendar

input nb: int

input nf: int

input n5: int

input n200: int

ask h_back: add_business(d, nb, cal_h)

ask h_fwd: add_business(d, nf, cal_h)

ask s_back: add_business(d, nb, cal)

ask s_fwd: add_business(d, nf, cal)

ask h_in: add_business(d, n5, cal_h)

ask h_in2: add_business(d, n200, cal_h)

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = 2026-06-01
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
  nb = -739768
  nf = 2912292
  n5 = 5
  n200 = 200

version v2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026
  known 2026-01-01
  cal_h = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
